    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1670">

                <pb facs="1322" n="1312" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg1312"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.991H/8–1049: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Vice Consul at Kunming</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lutkins</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kunming</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-08-10T09:00:00+07:00">August 10, 1949—9
                            a. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 12—3:56 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>122. ReDeptel 56, August 3, 7 p. m. Permission requested to inform in confidence
                    heads various mission groups of closure decision to give them adequate time for
                    making plans.</p>
                <p>CAT pilot tells me that closure common knowledge in Canton and Hong Kong. Though
                    I fear damage has been done, I am trying to plug leak with CAT here. Request
                    Canton do same.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 122, repeated Office of the Embassy, Canton 38.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lutkins</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
